{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/core_user/myprofile_category

    One card of the user profile.

    Facts are label and value pairs and come first; actions are the nodes that are only a
    link, and sit at the foot of the card under a rule. Core prints both in one flat list,
    which gives an email address and an "Edit profile" link the same weight.

    Neither the node title nor the node content is escaped, because neither is escaped by
    core's renderer either - both are pre-built HTML by contract. See the note in
    myprofile_renderer::node_context() for the plugin that proves the title half of that.

    A fact label and its value are kept on ONE source line each. Behat's I should see is a
    raw contains() over the element's string value with no whitespace normalisation, so a
    label broken across source lines cannot be asserted together with its value.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * title - Card heading.
    * classes - Extra CSS classes for the card.
    * hasfacts - Whether there is at least one fact.
    * facts - Array of nodes carrying content: name, title, hasurl, url, content, hasicon, iconhtml, classes.
    * hasactions - Whether there is at least one action.
    * actions - Array of link-only nodes: name, title, hasurl, url, hasicon, iconhtml, classes.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "User details",
        "classes": "node_category",
        "hasfacts": true,
        "facts": [
            {
                "name": "email",
                "title": "Email address",
                "hasurl": false,
                "url": "",
                "content": "aluno@example.org",
                "hasicon": false,
                "iconhtml": "",
                "classes": ""
            },
            {
                "name": "courseprofiles",
                "title": "Course details",
                "hasurl": false,
                "url": "",
                "content": "<ul><li>Human Rights in Professional Practice</li></ul>",
                "hasicon": false,
                "iconhtml": "",
                "classes": ""
            }
        ],
        "hasactions": true,
        "actions": [
            {
                "name": "editprofile",
                "title": "Edit profile",
                "hasurl": true,
                "url": "https://example.org/user/edit.php",
                "hasicon": false,
                "iconhtml": "",
                "classes": "editprofile"
            }
        ]
    }
}}
<section class="dimensions-profile-card {{classes}}">
    <h3 class="dimensions-profile-card-title">{{title}}</h3>
    {{#hasfacts}}
        <dl class="dimensions-profile-facts">
            {{#facts}}
                <div class="dimensions-profile-fact {{classes}}">
                    <dt class="dimensions-profile-fact-label">{{#hasurl}}<a href="{{url}}">{{{title}}}</a>{{/hasurl}}{{^hasurl}}{{{title}}}{{/hasurl}}{{#hasicon}} {{{iconhtml}}}{{/hasicon}}</dt>
                    <dd class="dimensions-profile-fact-value">{{{content}}}</dd>
                </div>
            {{/facts}}
        </dl>
    {{/hasfacts}}
    {{#hasactions}}
        <ul class="dimensions-profile-actions">
            {{#actions}}
                <li class="dimensions-profile-action {{classes}}">{{#hasurl}}<a href="{{url}}">{{{title}}}</a>{{/hasurl}}{{^hasurl}}<span>{{{title}}}</span>{{/hasurl}}{{#hasicon}} {{{iconhtml}}}{{/hasicon}}</li>
            {{/actions}}
        </ul>
    {{/hasactions}}
</section>
